<%#
  Devise sends this template for two different things:

  1. A NEW account (no pending reconfirmation). This email is the de facto
     invitation: Users::Creator creates users without a password and
     unconfirmed. When Google sign-in is on, Google is the primary action and
     "confirm and set a password" the secondary one.

     IMPORTANT -- the Google button links to the SIGN-IN PAGE, never straight to
     /users/auth/google_oauth2. OmniAuth 2.x refuses GET request-phase
     initiation, and an email link can only ever be a GET; the real POST button
     lives on the sign-in page. A new user who signs in with Google never needs
     the confirmation link: Users::OmniauthCallbacksController confirms them, and
     clears the token so this link stops working.

  2. An EMAIL ADDRESS CHANGE on an existing account (reconfirmable): the new
     address only takes effect once this link is clicked. No Google button --
     the point is to confirm the new address -- and wording that says so,
     rather than the "Welcome" copy, which made these look like they never
     arrived.

  Styles are inline because email clients do not load the asset pipeline.
%>
<% if @resource.pending_reconfirmation? %>
  <p>
    Hello <%= @name %>,
  </p>

  <p>
    Your BlueSky sign-in email address is being changed to <tt><%= @email %></tt>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Please click on the following link to confirm this new address. Until you do, you keep signing in with your current address:<br/>
    <%= link_to 'Confirm my new email address', confirmation_url(@resource, confirmation_token: @token) %>
  </p>

  <p>
    If you didn't expect this change, you can ignore this email, but please let a BlueSky administrator know.
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p>
    Hello <%= @name %>,
  </p>

  <p>
    Welcome to Bluesky, our lead management platform. Your login details are as follows:
  </p>

  <p>
    Username: <tt><%= @email %></tt>
  </p>

  <% if GoogleSignIn.enabled? %>
    <p style="margin: 28px 0 8px;">
      <a href="<%= new_user_session_url %>"
         style="display: inline-block; padding: 14px 28px; background-color: #005089; color: #ffffff;
                font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold;
                text-decoration: none; border-radius: 4px;">
        Sign in with Google
      </a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin: 0 0 24px; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #6c757d;">
      Use the Google account for <strong><%= @email %></strong>. No password needed.
    </p>

    <p style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">
      Prefer a password?
      <%= link_to 'Confirm my account and set a password', confirmation_url(@resource, confirmation_token: @token), style: 'color: #005089;' %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      Please click on the following link to complete setting up your account:<br/ >
      <%= link_to 'Confirm my account', confirmation_url(@resource, confirmation_token: @token) %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
